      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Remap playground - composable coordinate maps\n\ncv2.remap renders dst(p) = src(map_x(p), map_y(p)) from two HxW float32 coordinate arrays, and ANY geometric warp can be expressed this way. 'CV Identity Map' emits the do-nothing grid; every distortion node (Radial Lens, Cylinder, Pinch/Stretch, Wave, Displacement, Homography) REWRITES the coordinates flowing through it, so chaining nodes composes distortions - see the 'composed' branch, where a wave runs through the barrel map and both warps land in ONE resampling pass (no double interpolation loss). The maps are plain arrays: inspect them, or feed them through any NPARRAY math.\n\nTips: use borderMode=BORDER_CONSTANT on cv2_remap - BORDER_DEFAULT reflects image content into out-of-frame samples. The low-level registry also has cv2_warpPolar / cv2_linearPolar / cv2_logPolar (polar unwrap of dials and irises), cv2_initUndistortRectifyMap (calibrated camera undistortion) and cv2_convertMaps (fixed-point maps for speed). 'CV Homography Map' turns a 'Find Homography' matrix into a map so perspective + lens effects combine in one pass."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
